N5008 [class.derived.general]/2: "A class-or-decltype shall denote a
(possibly cv-qualified) class type that is not an incompletely defined
class"; X is incompletely defined in its own base-specifier-list.  The
front end crashed (SIGSEGV, unbounded recursion, bin53) instead of
reporting the error; it now reports "base class 'struct X' is incomplete".
test_class_template.desc and test_partial_specialization.desc (KNOWNBUG):
for a class template instance the same diagnostic is issued but, like any
ill-formed implicit instantiation of a user class template (a failing
static_assert, `T::nope x;' with T = int), tolerated, and verification
proceeds (accepts-invalid; no longer a crash).  g++ 13
("invalid use of incomplete type", "recursive type undefined") and
clang++ 18 ("circular inheritance") reject these programs.
